=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play updates/not-read ----------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: updates/not-read$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. A file in apt.conf.d with a$
# syntax error: apt-config dump fails, so the row is Unknown;$
# the item is offered, saying so, and refuses.$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [?] Auto Updates         Unknown can't read$
                           - Counted as not configured$
$
  Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [?] Upgrades             Can't read$
  [?] Package Lists        Can't read$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable automatic updates$
      Can't read apt's settings$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
# Warning$
# apt can't read its settings: Syntax error$
# /etc/apt/apt.conf.d/99site:1: Extra junk at end of file. Fix$
# that, then try again.$
$
# Auto Updates #################################################$
$
  [?] Auto Updates         Unknown can't read$
                           - Counted as not configured$
$
  Update Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [?] Upgrades             Can't read$
  [?] Package Lists        Can't read$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable automatic updates$
      Can't read apt's settings$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Enter your choice [0-1 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Nothing was applied.$
$

